# Reverse engineering — spec section 15.

gdb-multiarch
ltrace
strace
binutils
bless

# radare2 removed from this plain package list — confirmed (via
# packages.debian.org and its manpage's "other versions" listing) that
# it's available via bookworm-backports, NOT plain bookworm main. A
# .list.chroot file can't express "install from a specific suite" —
# that needs an explicit `-t bookworm-backports` apt flag, which only
# works from a shell command, not a plain package list. Moved to
# 0300-raptor-thirdparty-tools.hook.chroot, which enables backports
# transiently just for this one install rather than leaving the whole
# system pointed at backports by default (which would risk other
# packages silently pulling newer, less-tested backport versions).

# plain `gdb` intentionally not repeated here — already installed via
# raptor-development.list.chroot. gdb-multiarch kept explicit since it's
# RE-specific (cross-arch debugging) and dev doesn't need it by default.

# NOTE: Ghidra is not packaged for Debian — it ships as a standalone
# archive from its GitHub releases. If wanted, add it via a
# build/config/hooks/live/ hook that downloads and unpacks a pinned
# release, not this package list.
